  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "7sd/RK/o+Hp+dHhBceZytHBGbug=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:45.864Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Mesoneer AG delivers custom software and process automation from Zurich and also ships its own e-signature and identity products, with a fintech lean. That mix \u2014 services plus own products \u2014 is the finding, because the two halves imply different behaviour toward a third-party layer.\n\nThe services half is a straightforward carrier profile: custom software plus process automation is exactly where an append-only decision record attaches. The product half is the model the screen treats as a conflict elsewhere in the corpus, in Glintt's healthtech products and PinkRoccade's vertical software: a firm with its own roadmap answers a missing capability by building it, and a partner layer competes with a release plan it already sells.\n\nThe specific products sharpen the question rather than settling it. E-signature and identity are adjacent to decision provenance \u2014 signing and identity are how an approval is bound to a person \u2014 so there is a real chance of overlap with what the record layer asserts, and an equally real chance of complementarity, since the signature proves who acted while the record holds the ordered account of what was decided. Which of the two applies is the thing to establish before a pitch. Provenance: Flowable Partner Finder, mined 2026-08-18, not imprint-swept.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Mesoneer AG (CH Zurich) \u2014 mesoneer.io\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Custom software + process automation + own e-signature/ident products. Fintech-leaning \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:32:45.864087Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:45.864134Z"
    }
  },
